<title>UK: Shell says Nigeria oil workers dispute over.</title>
<headline>Shell says Nigeria oil workers dispute over.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>An oilworkers strike at Royal Dutch/Shell facilities in Nigeria has been resolved without any disruption to crude oil liftings, a Shell spokesman said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The strike, over an undisclosed pay issue, involved staff from Nigeria's two main oil unions Pengassan and Nupeng and started on Monday.</p>
<p>Shell management kept exports flowing from its Bonny and Forcados terminals without interruption.</p>
<p>-- Siobhan Hayden, London newsroom +44 171 542 8978</p>
